  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed a full-length set at the Fremont Theater in San Luis Obispo, California, on Friday, May 6, 2022 [1]. This specific capture, titled tmg2022-05-06, is the only available recording for this date and was taped and transferred by the uploader [1]. The audio is a matrix mix combining soundboard feed with audience microphones, resulting in a 91-minute file that documents the entire 23-song performance [1]. The setlist spans the band's extensive catalog, opening with “Have to Explode” from Tallahassee and “Corsican Mastiff Stride” from Getting Into Knives [1]. Notably, the group played “Abandoning My Father Talking Blues,” an unreleased track, which is a rare occurrence in their archived history [1][2]. The performance also included fan favorites like “Dance Music” and “Love Love Love” from The Sunset Tree, as well as “In Memory of Satan” from Transcendental Youth [1]. The show concluded with a five-song encore featuring “Song for Dennis Brown” and “No Children” [1]. The uploader describes the Fremont Theater as a super cool venue with standing room in the front and theater seats in the back, noting the palpable weight of history shared in that space [1]. This event is the 337th of 467 archived shows for the band, following their May 5, 2022, performance at The Warfield [2]. The uploader thanks Brandon Eggleston, management, the venue, and the band for supporting livetaping efforts [1].",
